          ":question/problem": "A marine rehabilitation aquarium initially houses $25$ marine animals. The number of animals in the aquarium $M(t)$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in months. If the maximum capacity of the aquarium is $60$ animals, which differential equation could be used to model the animal population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
