          ":question/problem": "A shipping company\u2019s management noted that the growth of a ship\u2019s speed is directly proportional to the difference between the ship\u2019s maximum cruising speed and its current speed. Let $V(t)$ be the speed of the ship, measured in kilometers per hour, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in hours. If the maximum cruising speed of the ship is $90$ $\\text{km/h}$, which differential equation could be used to model the ship\u2019s speed? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
